The Overkiz client (src/overkiz/) was written in JavaScript for this
project. It follows:
  - the public documentation of the TaHoma Developer Mode by Somfy
    (https://github.com/Somfy-Developer/Somfy-TaHoma-Developer-Mode): local
    API, mDNS announcement, token, Overkiz root CA;
  - pyoverkiz (https://github.com/iMicknl/python-overkiz-api), Copyright (c)
    2020 Mick Vleeshouwer, MIT License: Somfy account endpoints and the
    public client id and secret of the TaHoma app, cloud servers, local
    token creation, the mapping of Overkiz errors, state types;
  - the Overkiz integration of Home Assistant
    (https://github.com/home-assistant/core, homeassistant/components/
    overkiz), Apache License 2.0: which commands and states drive each kind
    of cover, the reserved positions 108 and 124.
The test fixtures (test/fixtures/setup.json, action-groups.json) are made
from the fixtures of pyoverkiz (MIT), with one PIN and new labels.

src/overkiz/overkiz-root-ca-2048.pem is the root certificate published by
Overkiz at https://ca.overkiz.com/overkiz-root-ca-2048.crt, unchanged.

